<title>UK: HORSE RACING-ROYAL ASCOT RESULTS.</title>
<headline>HORSE RACING-ROYAL ASCOT RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>ASCOT, England 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of feature races</p>
<p>on the final day of the four-day Royal Ascot meeting on Friday:</p>
<p>Hardwicke Stakes, a group two race for four-year-olds and</p>
<p>upwards, run over one and a half miles (2.4 kms)</p>
<p> 1. Predappio	    6-1 (ridden by Gary Stevens)</p>
<p> 2. Pilsudski	    2-1 favourite (Mick Kinane)</p>
<p> 3. Whitewater Affair 12-1 (Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p>10 Ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Half a length, two and a half lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by the Godolphin group and trained by Saeed Bin</p>
<p>Suroor in England.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 74,510 pounds sterling ($121,450).</p>
<p>King's Stand Stakes, group two race for three-year-olds and</p>
<p>upwards, run over five furlongs (1 km)</p>
<p> 1. Don't Worry Me   33-1 (Olivier Peslier)</p>
<p> 2. Titus Livius	7-1 co-favourite (Cash Asmussen)</p>
<p> 3. Hever Golf Rose   7-1 co-favourite (Pat Eddery)</p>
<p>18 ran. Almaty was the other 7-1 co-favourite.</p>
<p>Distances: A neck, one length.</p>
<p>Winner owned by J-F Gribomont and trained by Guy Henrot in</p>
<p>France.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 73,512 pounds sterling ($119,825).</p>
<p>King Edward VII Stakes, group two race for three-year-old</p>
<p>colts and geldings, run over one and a half miles (2.4 kms)</p>
<p>1. Kingfisher Mill  9-4 favourite (Pat Eddery)</p>
<p> 2. Falio Sky	  9-2 (Mick Kinane)</p>
<p>3. Musical Dancer  13-2 (Kieren Fallon)</p>
<p>Five ran.</p>
<p>Distances: Eight lengths, one and a half lengths.</p>
<p>Winner owned by Lord Howard de Walden and trained by Julie</p>
<p>Cecil at Newmarket in England.</p>
<p>Value to winner: 73,384 pounds sterling ($119,615).</p>
</text>
